    {
      "claim": "Ionized and zwitterionic features do not preclude F >= 20%: amlodipine showed 58% F and levodopa showed 71-86% F.",
      "card_ids": ["C17","C12","C14","C28","C29"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L6 hepatic clearance records are for other molecules (azosemide, diclofenac, GV150526, bumetanide, bupropion) and are not query-specific; they show mixed metabolism and cannot establish F < 20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C66","C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C75 shows bumetanide, a sulfonamide carboxylic acid secondary amine similar to the query, is not metabolized by CYP2E1, providing weak mechanistic support against major CYP mediated first-pass loss.",
      "card_ids": ["C75"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "C65 indicates monocarboxylic acid carrier transport of salicylic acid, a possible absorption mechanism for carboxylic acid containing molecules, but it is not query-specific.",
      "card_ids": ["C65"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "hepatic_clearance_metabolic_stability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C66","C67","C68","C69","C70","C71","C72","C73","C74","C75","C76","C77"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule is present in the supplied cards.",
    "No query-specific hepatic clearance or metabolic stability record is supplied; L6 records are for azosemide, bumetanide, diclofenac, GV150526, and bupropion.",
    "L6 clearance values are not matched to oral-versus-IV AUC ratios, so they cannot establish the F >= 20% threshold.",
    "Transfer from cirrhosis-context tolfenamic acid F values to a non-cirrhotic query is uncertain.",
    "First-pass extraction, food effects, formulation, and possible carrier-mediated absorption for the query are not resolved.",
    "The physicochemical prior does not account for possible active transport or saturable absorption mechanisms."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high. Direct human absolute F measurements for carboxylic acid analogs (diclofenac ~50%, tolfenamic acid ~91-100%) and other challenging carboxylic acid or sulfonamide drugs (telmisartan 42-58%, rigosertib ~35%, celecoxib 20-40%) support F >= 20%. L6 adds hepatic clearance records for other molecules (azosemide, diclofenac, GV150526) but none are query-specific and the direction is mixed; C75 shows structurally similar bumetanide is not a CYP2E1 substrate. L6 does not overturn the direct analog F evidence, so prediction remains high with low confidence."
}

